["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The same deer leaves a perfect print in mud, a hole in powder, and nothing on rock. Know the ground and you know what to trust.</p></aside><div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Snow: a whole trail to read.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snow: a whole trail to read. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Peter Cooper Jr., CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_tracks_in_snow_on_trail_at_McKinstry_Brook_WMA_2026-02-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-moose-tracks-mud.jpg\" alt=\"Mud: deep detail, slow to age.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Mud: deep detail, slow to age. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moose_Tracks_on_Seedskadee_National_Wildlife_Refuge_(22388750875).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-track-dirt.jpg\" alt=\"Dry ground: faint but readable.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Dry ground: faint but readable. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_tracks_near_Saddlerock_Wenatchee_Washington.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-tracks-shore.jpg\" alt=\"Shore mud: a herd came to drink.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Shore mud: a herd came to drink. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Loren Lane ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Many_elk_tracks_at_Clover_Lake_shore._101981._slide_(e7be1efbc1e74b41b6fce2ac2b030afb).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div>","<ul><li>Wet grounds show detail. Dry grounds hide it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Every ground ages at its own speed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this session covers</summary><ul><li><a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking/0\">Snow tracking</a> is the full snow method. <a href=\"#/s/rs-track-aging/0\">Aging tracks and sign</a> covers aging clocks. This session compares the grounds you will hunt: snow of every kind, mud, sand, dust, grass, leaves, duff and rock.</li><li>You will learn: what each ground shows and hides, snow types, melt out, mud traps, wet and dry sand, dust roads and the tire trick, reading leaf litter, natural track traps, and safety on snow and ice.</li><li>Your country: dusty grassland roads around Kamloops and the South Okanagan, mud and sand by Interior creeks and lakes, Fraser Valley mud and dyke edges, and November snow at Heffley Creek (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Key point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Wet snow captures detail; powder captures little <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Sun melts snow prints out bigger <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Mud shows toes and nails, and ages slowest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Wet sand shows detail; dry sand makes bowls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dust shows fine detail until the wind blows <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>No prints? Read flipped leaves, moss, duff, stones <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>A print on top of a tire mark came after the vehicle (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Crossings are natural track traps (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Detail follows.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 372\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Comparison of grounds. Wet snow: great detail, ages medium, beware melt out. Powder: blurry prints, depth only. Mud: great detail, ages slowest, looks fresh for days. Wet sand: good detail, edges dry fast. Dry sand: shapeless bowls, read the pattern. Dust: fine detail, wind erases it fast. Leaf litter: no prints, read disturbance.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"372\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Every ground, one table</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ground</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Detail</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ages</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"70\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"92.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wet snow</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"92.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">great</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">medium,</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">melts out</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"108\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1e6\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Powder</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">blurry</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">covered fast</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"146\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"168.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mud</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"168.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">great</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">slowest,</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">looks fresh</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"184\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1e6\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"206.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wet sand</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"206.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">good</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"206.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">edges dry fast</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"222\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dry sand</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">bowls only</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">fast</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"260\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1e6\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"282.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dust</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"282.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">fine</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"282.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">wind erases</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"298\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"320.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Leaves, duff</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"320.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">none</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"320.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">read disturbance</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"354\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Certainty 60 to 70%, see More</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Soft and damp grounds hold the best prints <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Track appearance varies hugely with ground and speed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the table in full</summary><ul><li>\"Depending on the substrate (snow, mud, dust, sand, etc.) and the speed the animal was moving, tracks may show great variability in their appearance\" (85%, Maine Inland Fisheries and Wildlife pocket card).</li><li>Mud: \"great for seeing the clear details in tracks like toes, pad shape and toenails\" and \"typically the slowest aging substrate\" (65%, Nature Mentor via search preview).</li><li>Sand: greatest detail when wet; edges dry fast in sun, wind and rain (65%, Nature Mentor and Point Reyes Light via search preview).</li><li>Dust: \"great detail can be seen in the fine grain of dust, but suitable tracks are rare\" (60%, search preview).</li><li>Small animals need finer, crisper ground than big ones to leave readable prints <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 306\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Snow types. Wet snow: sharp detail. Powder: holes with little detail. Crust: few prints, only scratches, and loud to walk on. Wind: fills and blurs tracks. The best day is a light fresh snow on firm ground.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"306\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow is not one ground</text>\n<rect x=\"16\" y=\"60\" width=\"180\" height=\"104\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\" stroke=\"#c7d3dd\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"106\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet snow</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sharp detail (85%)</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"60\" width=\"180\" height=\"104\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\" stroke=\"#c7d3dd\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Powder</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">holes, little detail</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"172\" width=\"180\" height=\"104\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe7ee\" stroke=\"#c7d3dd\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"106\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Crust</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">few prints, loud</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"172\" width=\"180\" height=\"104\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e6edf3\" stroke=\"#c7d3dd\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wind</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fills and blurs</text><g transform=\"translate(110 120) rotate(0) scale(0.9)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"298\" cy=\"120\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#c7d3dd\"/><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"233\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c7d3dd\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">scratch</text><ellipse cx=\"298\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#d5dee6\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#b8c6d2\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"284\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#b8c6d2\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"298\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#b8c6d2\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"218\" x2=\"332\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#b8c6d2\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Best day: a light fresh snow on firm ground</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Wet snow captures a print well; dry powder does not <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Crust: few prints and loud walking (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: snow types in full</summary><ul><li>\"Wet snow captures a paw print well, whereas dry powdery snow captures a less defined print pattern\" (85%, New York State Department of Environmental Conservation, Conservationist, February 2015).</li><li>\"A thin layer of wet snow shows the best tracks, but as the snow ages, the edges of the track will soften. Hard, crusty, or wet snow, or strong wind, can make tracks nearly empty\" (65%, search preview).</li><li>Powder: you read depth, spacing and drag marks, not shape (Tip).</li><li>Crust: animals may break through (deer) or walk on top (coyotes, hares). Your steps are loud; slow down or wait for a softer day (Tip).</li><li>Snow depth and movement: deer struggle past about 30 cm, moose to about 40 cm, elk between (65% to 75%, from <a href=\"#/s/food-water-cover/0\">Food, water and cover</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Aging a track in snow. Fresh: sharp walls and loose snow crumbs that fall apart when poked. Hours: crumbs bonded into a crust, trackers call it sintering. Sun: edges rounded, floor glazed. Wind or new snow: drifted in or filled. Ice floor and ice walls: made before last night's freeze. Cold clear nights keep tracks crisp for days, so trust the crumbs and your own test print.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aging a track in snow</text>\n  <g fill=\"#eef2f6\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <path d=\"M10 70 H34 V105 H70 V70 H94 V125 H10 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M108 70 H132 V105 H168 V70 H192 V125 H108 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M206 70 H222 Q234 76 236 98 Q240 105 250 105 Q262 105 264 98 Q266 76 278 70 H294 V125 H206 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M304 70 H322 Q330 84 334 96 Q348 100 362 96 Q366 84 374 70 H392 V125 H304 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"64\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"62\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"64\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"62\" r=\"3\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M116 66 q8 -6 16 0 M168 66 q8 -6 16 0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M238 104 Q250 100 262 104\" stroke=\"#9cc3e6\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M322 84 Q348 94 372 84\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"52\" y=\"150\">Fresh</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"150\">Hours</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"150\">Sun</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"150\">Wind, snow</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"52\" y=\"170\">loose crumbs</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"188\">sharp walls</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"170\">crumbs</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"188\">bonded</text>\n    <text x=\"250\" y=\"170\">rounded,</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"188\">glazed</text>\n    <text x=\"348\" y=\"170\">drifted</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"188\">or filled</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"208\" width=\"380\" height=\"120\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">Tests</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Poke a crumb: holds together means time passed</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Ice floor and walls: before last night's freeze</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Make your own print each hour: your clock</text>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\">Cold still nights keep tracks crisp for days</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: over five sunny days a deer print in snow melts out and grows bigger and rounder. A melted out fawn print can look like an elk print. Measure fresh prints only.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Melt out: prints grow</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"80\" width=\"400\" height=\"160\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#b8c6d2\"><animate attributeName=\"rx\" values=\"16;24;32\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;1\" begin=\"0.5s\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"ry\" values=\"22;30;40\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;1\" begin=\"0.5s\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"110\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#f2c94c\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.5s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">day 1</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.5s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">day 3</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.5s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">day 5</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.8s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"250\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c62828\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"271.6666666666667\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sun grows prints: a fawn can look like an elk</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Sun grows prints. Measure fresh ones. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>After sunny days a print can look much bigger and rounder <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>A melted out fawn print can fool you into \"elk\" (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: melt out in full</summary><ul><li>In snow \"an older track will increase in size and round off\" (65%, search preview); after a few days prints \"can appear huge with melting\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>South facing slopes melt prints fastest; north slopes keep them crisp (Tip).</li><li>Measure only crisp fresh prints, on the floor: <a href=\"#/s/rs-track-measuring/0\">Measuring tracks</a>.</li><li>Shape clues survive melt better than size: toe count, claws, pattern (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 306\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A print in mud, side view. The pushed up rim and the water seeping into the floor show it is fresh. Mud gives the best detail of toes, pads and nails, but it keeps a fresh look for days.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"306\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mud: detail and a trap</text>\n<path d=\"M20 120 H120 Q130 120 136 140 L150 200 H250 L264 140 Q270 120 280 120 H380 V250 H20 Z\" fill=\"#8a6f4e\" stroke=\"#5c4532\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"152\" y=\"186\" width=\"96\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">water seeps in</text><path d=\"M120 120 q8 -10 16 0 M264 120 q8 -10 16 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5c4532\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pushed up rim</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Best detail: toes, pads, nails (65%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c62828\" text-anchor=\"middle\">But mud keeps a fresh look for days (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Water seeping into the floor and a shiny rim: fresh (Tip).</li><li>Mud ages slowest: a crisp mud print can be days old <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: mud in full</summary><ul><li>In mud, fresh means the walls are still shiny and wet (Tip, from <a href=\"#/s/tracks/0\">Tracks</a>).</li><li>Morning frost freezes mud prints solid; they thaw and soften by afternoon (Tip).</li><li>Mud splashed onto clean leaves or rocks beside a crossing: something passed recently <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Elk rub wallow mud on nearby trees (65%, from <a href=\"#/s/sign/0\">Reading sign</a>).</li><li>Muddy creek crossings and pond edges in the Fraser Valley and Interior: check for webbed duck and goose tracks too (85% sizes). See <a href=\"#/s/rs-bird-sign/0\">Bird sign</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 296\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Wet sand holds a clear print shape. Dry loose sand slumps into a shapeless bowl. In dry sand read the spacing and pattern of the trail, not the print.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sand: wet tells, dry hides</text>\n<rect x=\"16\" y=\"62\" width=\"176\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#efe2c2\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"62\" width=\"176\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f6edd6\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet sand</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry sand</text><g transform=\"translate(104 160) rotate(0) scale(1.4)\" fill=\"#a8885a\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g><ellipse cx=\"296\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"#e3d2a8\" stroke=\"#c9b48a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">clear shape</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a shapeless bowl</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry sand: read the spacing, not the print</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Wet sand by water: clear shapes <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Dry sand: read the spacing and pattern, not the print (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sand in full</summary><ul><li>Sand \"holds tracks well\", but \"its edges dry out fast\", so freshness checks look at whether the raised edges are still moist (65%, Point Reyes Light via search preview).</li><li>Wind ripples fill dry sand prints within hours on an exposed bar (Tip).</li><li>Lake beaches and river bars are classic places to learn tracks: walk them at dawn (Tip).</li><li>In dry sand the gait still shows: <a href=\"#/s/rs-track-measuring/0\">Measuring tracks and reading gait patterns</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a tire track crosses a dirt road. Then a deer crosses, and its hoof print sits on top of the tire tread. A print on top of the tire mark was made after the vehicle passed.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Who was first?</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"70\" width=\"400\" height=\"180\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dccaa3\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.3s\" dur=\"0.6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"120\" width=\"400\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b9a57e\"/><rect x=\"4\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"52\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"68\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"84\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"116\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"132\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"148\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"164\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"196\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"212\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"244\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"260\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"276\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"292\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"308\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"324\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"356\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"372\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/><rect x=\"388\" y=\"122\" width=\"8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#a8936b\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.6s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tire track</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.6s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g transform=\"translate(150 220) rotate(20) scale(0.7)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.1s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g transform=\"translate(170 180) rotate(20) scale(0.7)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.6s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g transform=\"translate(190 136) rotate(20) scale(0.7)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.1s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g transform=\"translate(210 96) rotate(20) scale(0.7)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><path d=\"M-2 -20 C-9 -16 -13 -2 -12 12 C-11 19 -3 20 -2 14 Z\"/><path d=\"M2 -20 C9 -16 13 -2 12 12 C11 19 3 20 2 14 Z\"/></g></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.8s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"256\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"277.6666666666667\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Print on top of the tire: crossed after the truck</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>On top came last: a print over a tire was made after the truck. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Dust shows fine detail, until the wind blows <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>A print on top of a tire tread: made after that vehicle passed (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: dust and roads in full</summary><ul><li>In fine dust a fresh print has a thin raised rim that collapses within hours (60%, from <a href=\"#/s/tracks/0\">Tracks</a>).</li><li>The overlap rule: whatever mark lies on top was made last. A track printed over a tire tread came after the vehicle; a tread over a track came after the animal (Tip, simple logic).</li><li>If you know when a vehicle passed (yours, last evening), the overlap brackets the age of the track (Tip).</li><li>Dusty grassland roads near Kamloops: drive slowly at first light and look for fresh crossings, then come back on foot (Tip). Never shoot from or across a road; see the Rule Book.</li><li>Dust bowls from grouse and quail: <a href=\"#/s/rs-bird-sign/0\">Bird sign</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 296\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"In leaf litter, duff and rock, look for what moved: a flipped leaf showing its pale or wet side, scuffed moss torn green inside, pressed duff making a dark dent, or a stone with its damp side up.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No prints? Read what moved</text>\n<rect x=\"16\" y=\"62\" width=\"180\" height=\"88\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"106\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flipped leaf</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pale or wet side up</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"62\" width=\"180\" height=\"88\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scuffed moss</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">torn, green inside</text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"162\" width=\"180\" height=\"88\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"106\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pressed duff</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a dark dent</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"162\" width=\"180\" height=\"88\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"294\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moved stone</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">damp side up</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No prints? Read what moved (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Leaves, duff and rock show disturbance, not prints <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Crouch low and look along the ground toward the light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: litter, grass and rock in full</summary><ul><li>Sign of passage in litter: \"displaced vegetation or stones\", \"turned over leaves\", \"dew knocked off vegetation\", broken cobwebs (65%, tracking glossary via search preview).</li><li>Grass: bent stems lie the way the animal moved (65%, from <a href=\"#/s/tracks/0\">Tracks</a>). A dark line through dewy grass is a fresh trail (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/rs-track-aging/0\">Aging tracks and sign</a>.</li><li>Rock: look for scuffs of soil carried onto clean rock, moss scraped off, pebbles knocked out of their beds (Tip).</li><li>Use low side light: <a href=\"#/s/rs-track-following/0\">Following a track</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map of natural track traps: where a creek and a dirt road cross, where a fence line meets the road, and creek and fence crossings. Tracks pile up at crossings.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Natural track traps</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"380\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e9efe0\"/><path d=\"M10 200 Q140 170 220 200 T390 180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cbb994\" stroke-width=\"18\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dirt road</text><path d=\"M120 60 Q100 160 130 270\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">creek</text><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 6\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fence line</text><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"195\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"190\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"120\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"130\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Circles: crossings where tracks pile up (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Creek crossings, road edges, fence lines and field edges collect tracks (Tip).</li><li>Check them first on any new piece of ground (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: traps in full</summary><ul><li>Animals funnel through the easy places: low spots in fences, shallow creek crossings, gaps in brush. Those are where prints pile up (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/funnels/0\">Trails and funnels</a>.</li><li>Fence crossings collect hair too (65%, from <a href=\"#/s/sign/0\">Reading sign</a>).</li><li>Road edges: walk the soft shoulder of a quiet forest service road (FSR) at first light. Read which way crossings go and how fresh they are (Tip).</li><li>Smooth a strip of dirt on a trail with your boot one evening and check it in the morning: a homemade track trap (Tip).</li><li>Private land and consent rules still apply at fences <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. See <a href=\"#/s/maps-land-status/0\">Maps: land status</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Avalanche terrain. Slopes around 30 degrees and steeper can slide once there is enough snow. Open slopes, gullies and the run out zone below them are all danger. Gentle, treed ground is safer. Take an Avalanche Skills Training level 1 course before you hunt steep snow.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche terrain</text>\n  <path d=\"M20 250 L230 250 L380 60 L380 250 Z\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M230 250 L380 60\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120 250 L230 250\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M265 250 A 35 35 0 0 0 258 228\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">30 degrees +</text>\n  <path d=\"M320 120 L300 160 M340 110 L310 190\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"end\">can slide</text>\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">run out</text>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,250 40,220 50,250\"/><polygon points=\"60,250 70,215 80,250\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"55\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">gentle, treed</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche Skills Training 1: 2 days, before steep snow</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Avalanche terrain starts around 30 degrees once there is enough snow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>November river and lake ice is not trustworthy (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: safety in full</summary><ul><li>Avalanche terrain starts around 30 degrees of slope once there is enough snow to slide. Open slopes, gullies and the run outs below them can slide in November (70%, from <a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking/0\">Snow tracking</a>).</li><li>Check the Avalanche Canada forecast before snow country trips (Tip).</li><li>Do not cross river or lake ice to save a kilometre (Tip). Cold water: <a href=\"#/s/water-safety/0\">Water safety</a>.</li><li>Set a turnaround time; leave a trip plan (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety/0\">Bush safety</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-trail-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Know the ground before you trust the track.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Know the ground before you trust the track. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Loren Lane ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elk_tracks_in_snow._111984._slide_(ba1503e681a9402f97f934fbd6d8a5d8).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law): Ask the ground how honest it is before you ask the track how old it is.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Measuring a melted out snow print and calling it an elk.</li><li>Calling a crisp mud print fresh because it looks perfect.</li><li>Giving up on leaf litter because there are no prints.</li></ul></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map of natural track traps: where a creek and a dirt road cross, where a fence line meets the road, and creek and fence crossings. Tracks pile up at crossings.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Natural track traps</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"380\" height=\"210\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e9efe0\"/><path d=\"M10 200 Q140 170 220 200 T390 180\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cbb994\" stroke-width=\"18\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dirt road</text><path d=\"M120 60 Q100 160 130 270\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">creek</text><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 6\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fence line</text><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"195\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"190\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"120\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"130\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Circles: crossings where tracks pile up (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Find one deer print in 3 different grounds: mud, dust or sand, and snow or grass. Photograph each with your knife. Compare detail and age.</p></aside>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"rs-ss-check\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"rs-ss-check:0\"><span>Print found in mud</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"rs-ss-check:1\"><span>Print found in dust or sand</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"rs-ss-check:2\"><span>Print or trail found in snow or grass</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"rs-ss-check:3\"><span>One natural track trap checked at dawn</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"rs-ss-check:4\"><span>A tire overlap read on a dirt road</span></label></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 292\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Memory hooks. Wet tells, dry hides: wet snow, mud and wet sand show detail. Sun grows snow prints: measure fresh prints only. On top came last: a print over a tire mark was made after the truck.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"292\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Memory hooks</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"60\" width=\"360\" height=\"66\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet tells, dry hides</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet snow, mud, wet sand show detail</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"136\" width=\"360\" height=\"66\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sun grows snow prints</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Measure fresh prints only</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"212\" width=\"360\" height=\"66\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">On top came last</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Print over tire: after the truck</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Wet tells, dry hides.</strong></li><li><strong>Sun grows snow prints.</strong></li><li><strong>On top came last.</strong></li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>M S D L</strong>: Mud, Sand, Dust, Leaves. Each has its own trap: too fresh looking, shapeless, wind erased, no prints.</li><li>\"Crossings collect\": check every creek, fence and road crossing.</li><li>\"Powder shows depth, wet snow shows toes.\"</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>New York State Department of Environmental Conservation, <a href=\"https://extapps.dec.ny.gov/docs/administration_pdf/tracks1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Winter Tracks, Conservationist February 2015</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>: wet versus powder snow.</li></ul><ul><li>Maine Inland Fisheries and Wildlife, <a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/IFW/docs/MDIFW-Animal-Tracking-Card-color.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pocket guide to Maine animal tracks</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>: substrate variability.</li></ul><ul><li>Search previews, checked 2026-10-11, capped at 60% to 65%: <a href=\"https://nature-mentor.com/find-animal-tracks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nature Mentor, where to find animal tracks</a> and <a href=\"https://nature-mentor.com/how-to-tell-if-animal-tracks-are-fresh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">how to tell if tracks are fresh</a>; <a href=\"https://www.ptreyeslight.com/?p=66939\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Point Reyes Light, tracking</a>; <a href=\"https://www.lib.niu.edu/2002/oi020805.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Northern Illinois University, tracking</a>; <a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/survival/animal-tracks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, animal tracks</a>; <a href=\"https://www.huntingbc.ca/forum/archive/index.php/t-29633.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunting BC forum archive</a> and <a href=\"https://forums.bowhunting.com/threads/how-old-is-this-buck-based-on-his-track.89036/page-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">bowhunting forum</a> (melt out); <a href=\"https://bear-tracker.com/glossary.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bear Tracker glossary</a>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Snow depth, avalanche and ice lines as sourced in <a href=\"#/s/food-water-cover/0\">Food, water and cover</a> and <a href=\"#/s/snow-tracking/0\">Snow tracking</a>.</li></ul><ul><li>Research log: <code>research/2026-10-11-rs.md</code>.</li></ul>"]